---
description: CCC Data/AI contest repo, project rules for Cursor agents
alwaysApply: true
---
This repo is shared by a Claude Code user (iustin, contest driver) and a Cursor user (gurita, second opinion).

- `CLAUDE.md` is the project instruction file for every agent, not only Claude: read it first and follow its Rules.
- Your signature is in `.claude/signature.local` (gitignored). Commits: subject `[<signature>] <what changed>`,
  trailer `Signed-off-by: <signature>`, no AI attribution lines. `git pull --rebase` before every push, never force-push `main`.
- `.claude/skills/*/SKILL.md` are plain markdown playbooks. When CLAUDE.md says "invoke the X skill", read
  `.claude/skills/X/SKILL.md` and follow it. `ccc-ai-context` = session start, `ccc-ai-solve` + `ccc-ai-patterns` = solving a level.
- Only the contest driver (see `docs/team/roles.md`) runs golive, `ccc.py go`, `submit` or `fetch` for the contest. The
  second opinion works in shadow mode (`docs/strategy/shadow-prompt.md`, `arena/duo.py`) and only writes inside its own
  run folder `arena/runs/<run>-<signature>/`.
- Never commit `arena/.auth/` (credentials, cookies) or files over 50 MB. Never ask the user to paste a password into chat.
- Talk to the other teammate's agent through `docs/team/handoff.md` (format in `docs/team/protocol.md`).
